        { "host": "A", "text": "And?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "They all achieve a recall of below 21% and a precision of less than 9%. Stronger models increase recall from 8% to 17%, but they do not improve precision." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "The twist is in the title: agents find different bugs than maintainers fix. The paper says evaluators still judge 85% of the findings valid, so low precision here isn't the same as a worthless finding." },
