      "type": "item",
      "section": "Frontier models & labs",
      "headline": "Google releases Gemini 4 Carbon to a subset of cyber defenders, claiming 59 on Artificial Analysis v5.0",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Google released Gemini 4 Carbon, and the first people to get it are not developers. Google says it will make Carbon available to a subset of cyber defenders, expanding gradually through what it calls the Fairwind Program." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "What is it claiming for it?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Google says Carbon ranks number 1 on the updated version 5.0 of the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, with a score of 59. On security benchmarks it reports a state-of-the-art 88.2% on SEC-bench Pro, 54.8% on ExploitGym, and 71.0% on CWE-bench." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "And the prompt-injection number from the intro?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "On the Gray Swan prompt-injection benchmark Google says Carbon achieves 0.0%, resisting every evaluated attack attempt." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Worth saying clearly: every one of those figures is Google's own company claim, not independently verified. The post names no independent evaluation, and it gives no date for developer or public availability." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "transition",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "To the papers, and two results about what coding agents can and can't do." }
      ]
